# Layered Architecture for Express APIs

Every feature must be split across five layers. Never skip or merge layers.

## Layer Responsibilities

| Layer | File | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| Model | `models/*.model.ts` | TypeScript types/interfaces only — no logic |
| Repository | `repositories/*.repository.ts` | All storage access — no business logic |
| Service | `services/*.service.ts` | Business logic only — no HTTP, no storage calls |
| Controller | `controllers/*.controller.ts` | HTTP only: parse req → call service → send res |
| Router | `routes/*.routes.ts` | Wire controller methods to Express routes |

## Rules

- **Services** never import from `express` and never touch storage directly
- **Controllers** never contain `if/else` business logic — delegate everything to the service
- **Repositories** expose named query methods (`findById`, `save`, `findPaginated`) — no raw storage outside the repo
- **Routers** are factory functions `createXRouter(controller, ...middleware): Router`
- **Models** are plain `interface` / `type` definitions — no classes, no methods

## Correct structure

```
src/
  models/        traffic.model.ts       ← types only
  repositories/  traffic.repository.ts  ← storage access
  services/      traffic.service.ts     ← business logic
  controllers/   traffic.controller.ts  ← HTTP layer
  routes/        traffic.routes.ts      ← routing
  schemas/       traffic.schema.ts      ← input validation (Zod etc.)
```

## Anti-patterns

```typescript
// ❌ service touches express
import { Request } from 'express';
export class TrafficService {
  handle(req: Request) { ... }
}

// ❌ controller contains business logic
ingestTraffic(req, res) {
  const existing = this.repo.findByName(req.body.app); // NO — go through service
  if (existing) { existing.count++; }
}

// ❌ service queries storage directly
export class TrafficService {
  private cache = new LRUCache(...); // NO — use a repository
}

// ❌ route handler inline in router file
router.post('/traffic', (req, res) => {
  const record = { ...req.body, id: uuid() }; // NO — move to controller + service
});
```

## Repository contract

Every repository must implement:
- `save(entity)` — persist
- `findById(id)` — single lookup
- `findAll()` / `findPaginated(page, limit)` — bulk reads
- `count()` — aggregate
- `clear()` — test teardown
